@format 1
@id preview.open-media
@title Open media
@area Preview
@entry input
@summary Resolve the selected media, attempt FFprobe and Flyleaf independently, commit the new availability state, and synchronize the timeline.
@flow TB
@related preview.waveform-generation, split.sidecar-restore
@tag media
@tag flyleaf
@tag ffprobe

@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias preference = Cadroue.UIShell.LPreference
@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[input] Media open request <input>
- Receive a source path from the user, drop target, list, relay, or session restore @ viewer.PViewerSourceOpen(...)
> resolve

[resolve] Resolve source <decision>
- Resolve a sidecar to its media source when needed @ viewer.PViewerSidecarResolve(...)
- Record the source as the last opened media @ preference.LPreferenceMediaSet(...)
? "A usable media path is available" > probe
? "Sidecar resolution is rejected or fails" > rejected

[probe] Probe the media <decision>
- Attempt to read media information with FFprobe @ viewer.PPlayerVideoLoad(...)
? "Audio-only media is outside the Audio tab" > unavailable
? "FFprobe returns information" > preview
? "FFprobe fails" > preview

[preview] Attempt preview opening <process>
- Create or reuse a Flyleaf player, then attempt to open and pause the source @ viewer.PPlayerVideoLoad(...)
> commit

[unavailable] Commit an unavailable source <process>
- Commit a new source status with neither processing nor preview availability @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
> timeline

[commit] Commit preview state <process>
- Swap or retain the player and bind it to the host @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
- Reset playback and non-persistent crop state @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
- Apply autoplay or an initial paused frame @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
- Publish the media status to the active workspace @ viewer.PViewerMediaRaise(...)
> timeline

[timeline] Apply media status to the timeline <decision>
- Receive the committed media status @ window.PWindowMediaHandle(...)
? "FFprobe supplied media information" > attach
? "No media information is available" > clear

[attach] Initialize timeline for the source <process>
- Attach media duration, cursor, sections, keyframes, and waveform work @ flow.PFlowAttach(...)
> result

[clear] Clear the current timeline <process>
- Clear timeline media and suspend its keyframe work @ flow.PFlowClear(...)
> result

[result] New media state committed <output>
= The new source can be processable-only, preview-only, available to both, or unavailable to both. Flyleaf or FFprobe failure does not retain the previous media; no FFprobe information clears the timeline.

[rejected] Sidecar opening rejected <error>
= The previous preview and timeline state remain active.
